    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[FF144 CSSStyleProperties docs]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41254</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41254"/>
        <updated>2025-09-30T06:29:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">FF144 (and Safari) implement <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code>. This is a derived class of <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> that represents the inline or computed styles on an element. It exists because  <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code> is now going to be a base class from which specific types of style and rule information will be applied, and only include the relevant information for that context.</p>
<p dir="auto">Anyway, this adds the new class and fixes up all the places that return it. It also updates  <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleDeclaration</code>  to note that this is now a base class but didn't used to be.</p>
<p dir="auto">There is quite a lot of duplication. Mostly because there was before I started too. I wasn't sure how much to include in say <code class="notranslate">HTMLElement.style</code> and how much to have in the <code class="notranslate">CSSStyleProperties</code> as common. Generally I have kept about the same level in each doc as originally.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3417388824" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/41133/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41133">#41133</a></p>]]></content>
